# Build-time config for any production build of the web app.
#
# Committed on purpose, and it holds no secrets: a public API address is not
# one, and it is visible in the shipped bundle either way.
#
# It lives here rather than in the host's dashboard because Vite bakes this in
# at build time, so a value added to the host later has no effect until the
# next build. Cloudflare also refuses to accept variables at all on a Worker
# that only serves static assets, which is exactly what this project deploys.
# Keeping it in the repository makes the build reproducible anywhere.
#
# Vite loads this automatically for `vite build`, layered over .env, so local
# development still uses the localhost API from .env.
VITE_API_URL=https://craftbid-api.onrender.com
